    {
      "q": "How much federal contract money goes to New Mexico?",
      "a": "Answer: New Mexico has received $1.6B in federal contract obligations in FY2027 to date. The total comes from 504 awards with an average award size of $3.1M, and obligations are down 90.0% year over year."
    },
    {
      "q": "Which agencies award the most contracts in New Mexico?",
      "a": "Answer: The Department of Energy awards the most contracts in New Mexico, with $1.5B in obligations in FY2027 to date. The Department of Veterans Affairs follows with $19.8M and the Department of Health and Human Services with $17M."
